# AI Capsule - environment variable template
#
# Copy this file to backend/.env for local development:
#     cp .env.example backend/.env
# then fill in real values. backend/.env is git-ignored and must never be committed.
#
# On the cloud platform these are set as Application Settings / environment variables.
# Only the NAMES are documented in the README - never the values.

# --- Required ---------------------------------------------------------------

# Signs and verifies the application JWT (the session cookie named "token").
# Use a long random string, e.g. `node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(48).toString('hex'))"`
JWT_SECRET=replace-with-a-long-random-string

# GitHub OAuth App credentials.
# GitHub -> Settings -> Developer settings -> OAuth apps -> your app.
# The client ID is public (it appears in the authorize URL).
# The client secret is NOT public - keep it out of git, chat and the README.
GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=your-github-oauth-app-client-id
GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=replace-with-your-client-secret

# --- Optional ---------------------------------------------------------------

# Where the SQLite file lives.
# Local default: backend/data/capsules.db
# Azure App Service: /home/data/capsules.db  (persistent mount, outside wwwroot)
# DATABASE_PATH=

# Set automatically by the cloud platform; 3001 is used locally.
# PORT=3001

# "production" enables Secure cookies. Leave unset locally so the app works over http.
# NODE_ENV=production

# Absolute base URL used to build the OAuth callback URL.
# Leave unset and the app derives it from the incoming request, which works both
# locally (http://localhost:3001) and on Azure (https://<app>.azurewebsites.net).
# APP_URL=
